BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kpa-20261130-0@kpa.energy
DTSTAMP:20261029T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
SUMMARY:Stanton 1 emergency order expires
DESCRIPTION:DOE Order 202-26-42 keeps Orlando's Stanton Unit 1 available th
 rough 30 November\; no renewal had been posted by 25 November. Stanton 1 r
 an at 43% in January–August 2026 under orders. https://kpa.energy/findin
 gs/#ordered-vs-kept-22
URL:https://kpa.energy/findings/#ordered-vs-kept-22
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kpa-20261201-1@kpa.energy
DTSTAMP:20261029T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Winter 2026–27 begins\, the season KPA's calls test
DESCRIPTION:KPA call CS-1: across ERCOT's 10 highest net-load hours\, Decem
 ber 2026 to February 2027\, battery output averages less than 30% of batte
 ry capacity in service (Likely\, 70%). It was 24% in winter 2025 and 7% in
  2025–26. https://kpa.energy/findings/#fern-ten-hours-7
URL:https://kpa.energy/findings/#fern-ten-hours-7
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kpa-20261203-2@kpa.energy
DTSTAMP:20261029T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261203
SUMMARY:GE Vernova CEO at Goldman Sachs conference
DESCRIPTION:First public remarks since the third-quarter release\, when gas
  backlog and slot reservations stood at 122 GW. KPA call SM-1 needs about 
 8 GW more by year-end. https://kpa.energy/findings/#gev-book-122
URL:https://kpa.energy/findings/#gev-book-122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kpa-20261209-3@kpa.energy
DTSTAMP:20261029T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261209
SUMMARY:PJM 2029/30 capacity auction opens
DESCRIPTION:Bidding runs 9–15 December under a $337.83/MW-day cap and $18
 1.91 floor\, with a 158\,712 MW reliability requirement. It settles KPA ca
 ll LB-1: a clear at the price cap. https://kpa.energy/findings/#pjm-price
URL:https://kpa.energy/findings/#pjm-price
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kpa-20261211-4@kpa.energy
DTSTAMP:20261029T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261211
SUMMARY:Centralia 2 emergency order expires
DESCRIPTION:DOE Order 202-26-44 keeps TransAlta's Centralia Unit 2 availabl
 e through 11 December. The unit ran at 0% in January–August 2026. https:
 //kpa.energy/findings/#ordered-vs-kept-22
URL:https://kpa.energy/findings/#ordered-vs-kept-22
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kpa-20261218-5@kpa.energy
DTSTAMP:20261029T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261218
SUMMARY:Schahfer and Culley emergency orders expire
DESCRIPTION:DOE Orders 202-26-46 and 202-26-47 hold 812 MW in Indiana throu
 gh 18 December. If Schahfer's 722 MW retired this month along with Sherco 
 1 and Comanche 2\, 2026 coal retirements would pass 1.5 GW and KPA call BF
 -1 would fail. https://kpa.energy/findings/#retired-2025-2-7
URL:https://kpa.energy/findings/#retired-2025-2-7
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kpa-20261222-6@kpa.energy
DTSTAMP:20261029T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261222
SUMMARY:PJM 2029/30 auction results
DESCRIPTION:PJM posts results for the auction that closes 15 December. A cl
 ear at $337.83/MW-day resolves KPA call LB-1 as correct. https://kpa.energ
 y/findings/#pjm-price
URL:https://kpa.energy/findings/#pjm-price
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kpa-20261223-7@kpa.energy
DTSTAMP:20261029T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261223
SUMMARY:EIA Form 860M for November 2026
DESCRIPTION:The first inventory after Campbell's planned November retiremen
 t date\; the October inventory showed 0 MW of US coal retired in 2026 and 
 3.6 GW still dated to retire this year. https://kpa.energy/findings/#retir
 ed-2025-2-7
URL:https://kpa.energy/findings/#retired-2025-2-7
END:VEVENT
